<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST- HUNGARY T-BILL, GOVT BOND YIELDS SEEN UP.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- HUNGARY T-BILL, GOVT BOND YIELDS SEEN UP.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian discount Treasury bill and government bond yields are seen rising at this weeks auctions, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Government Debt Management Agency will auction one-month T-bills on Tuesday, three-month T-bills on Wednesday, two-year government bonds of the 1999/F series and five-year bonds of the 2001/C series on Thursday.</p>
<p>		   ONE-MONTH    THREE-MONTH   TWO-YEAR FIVE-YEAR</p>
<p>		     T-BILL	  T-BILL	  BOND	 BOND</p>
<p>Offered amount</p>
<p>   (HUF billion)    1		 5	     20	   5</p>
<p>Average yield at</p>
<p>   last auction    21.18	   20.64	  18.58     15.69</p>
<p>			(Feb 18)	(Feb 19)     (Jan 30)  (Jan 30)</p>
<p>Valid bid</p>
<p>   range	  19.18-22.18   18.64-21.24	-	    -</p>
<p> Maximum bid	   -		 -	    19.08     16.19</p>
<p>FORECASTS OF HUNGARIAN DEALERS Tamas Puskas/Raiffeisen Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	  21.20	   20.60	  18.50     15.70</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	  21.50	   20.80	  18.70     15.95</p>
<p>Robert Keszthelyi/Daiwa-MKB</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	  21.20	   20.70	  18.65     16.05</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	  21.45	   20.85	  18.80     16.10</p>
